{
  "info": {
    "name": "Builder Plaza API",
    "description": "Testing evidence collection for dev doc §17.4 / assignment 'Automated System Testing'. Run 'Auth > Dev login' first (local/test backend only, environment=local) to populate {{token}}; most other requests inherit it via collection-level Bearer auth. Set {{other_user_id}} manually to a second user's id (e.g. copy owner_id from a GET /projects response, or dev-login a second github_login and copy user.id) before running the Matches/Trust/Requests folders -- there is no generic user-search endpoint. GitHub/LinkedIn OAuth *callback* requests are included for API-contract completeness only; they need a real code/state from the provider and will 400 if run directly.\n\nVerified 2026-07-20 with `newman run` against a local backend (fresh Postgres+pgvector, migrated, no seed data): 57/58 requests behaved exactly as documented (the one failure is the LinkedIn-callback redirect target, localhost:3000, not running in that environment -- expected). Two things to know when running the whole collection with a single {{token}}: (1) 'accept'/'decline' on a request you sent yourself correctly 403 -- that's the ownership rule working, not a bug; run those as the recipient's token to see 200. (2) POST /users/{id}/reviews needs {{request_id}} to point at an ACCEPTED request, so run the Requests & Conversations folder (as both parties) before Trust & Evidence if you want that one to succeed rather than 422 on an empty id.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8000" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "project_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "posting_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "request_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "conversation_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "match_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "other_user_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "internal_task_token", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "request": { "auth": { "type": "noauth" }, "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/health" }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /health/db",
          "request": { "auth": { "type": "noauth" }, "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/health/db" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth (F1 Dual-Source Trust Gateway)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Dev login (local/test only)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.access_token);",
                  "  pm.test('token captured', () => pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"github_login\": \"demo-builder\",\n  \"primary_role\": \"builder\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/dev-login"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GitHub connect (real public GitHub data)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().access_token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"github_login\": \"torvalds\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/github/connect"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/linkedin/mode",
          "request": { "auth": { "type": "noauth" }, "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/linkedin/mode" }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/linkedin/profiles (simulated only)",
          "request": { "auth": { "type": "noauth" }, "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/linkedin/profiles" }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /auth/linkedin/bind (simulated only)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"profile_id\": \"li_ryan\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/linkedin/bind"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/linkedin/login (live OIDC authorize URL)",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/linkedin/login" }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/github/login (browser redirect)",
          "request": { "auth": { "type": "noauth" }, "method": "GET", "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/github/login" }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/github/callback (reference only -- needs real code/state)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/github/callback?code=REPLACE_ME&state=REPLACE_ME"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/linkedin/callback (reference only -- needs real code/state)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/linkedin/callback?code=REPLACE_ME&state=REPLACE_ME"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
